note ngbench: the Hive NG A/B timing harness (seed/ng/ngbench.om). Built by seed/out/omc; it builds
note nothing itself. It runs already-built arm binaries in palindromic ABBA blocks, times each process
note with monons from before fork to after waitpid, checks every output against its referee hash and
note checks every arm binary's identity before and after timing. It writes raw rows only; the
note statistics are done in Wolfram from the rows. Base: bench/omc_efficiency/conductor.om (omega-mv
note perf/omc-efficiency-baseline d11a7177): child, runone, packet and row code ported from it.
note
note ngbench sum FILE ..
note     one line per FILE: 64 lowercase hex digits of its SHA-256, two spaces, FILE (the format of
note     sha256sum). Exit 0, or 1 when a FILE cannot be read (named on stderr).
note ngbench run BLOCKS WARM DIR ARM .. -- CASE ..
note     DIR/bin/ARM/CASE   the arm binary (absent and unlisted: the pair is skipped)
note     DIR/manifest.sha256  sha256sum lines "HEX  bin/ARM/CASE" for every present binary
note     DIR/want/CASE.sha256 the referee's stdout SHA-256 (64 hex digits)
note     DIR/in/CASE        optional stdin of every run of CASE (else /dev/null)
note     DIR/run.out DIR/run.err  scratch files: the child's stdout and stderr
note   ARM names state their kind by prefix: omc (the seeded omc layout: AArch64 ELF, entry 0x4000b0,
note   no section table, no "GCC: (" string), gcc (an AArch64 ELF holding "GCC: ("), ng (an AArch64
note   ELF without "GCC: ("). Any other prefix is a usage error.
note   Identity, before any timing: every present binary must match its kind, be listed in the manifest
note   with its own SHA-256; a binary listed but absent is refused. After the last block every binary is
note   hashed again and must be unchanged. A failed identity check is refused by name, no run is timed.
note   Order: block b (0 .. WARM+BLOCKS-1), for every CASE: the present arms p0 .. pk-1 rotated left by
note   b, then the same sequence reversed (A B B A for two arms), so every arm runs twice per block at
note   mirrored positions. Blocks below WARM are warm-up, flagged warm=1.
note Rows (stdout, one per line, space separated):
note   H ngbench v2 blocks=B warm=W cpus=LIST core=N|unpinned clustermask=M load=LOADAVG
note   A CASE ARM SHA256 BYTES | A CASE ARM absent      I CASE SHA256 BYTES (stdin file)
note   L BLOCK LOADAVG          at every block start
note   T BLOCK WARM CASE ARM POS WALL_NS STATUS OK INPROC_NS
note     STATUS: exit status, or 1000+signal; OK 1 only when STATUS is 0 and the stdout SHA-256 equals
note     the want; INPROC_NS: the child's stderr when it is exactly one decimal line, else 0
note   v2 contamination rows (seed/ng/bench/PREREG-contamination.md), only when ngbench is pinned to one
note   CPU (Cpus_allowed_list a single number N; the cluster is cpuN/topology/cluster_cpus_list).
note   Before (PH s) and after (PH e) the ABBA sequence of every BLOCK and CASE, every task of
note   /proc/*/task/*/stat is read (field 3 state, field 39 last processor); ngbench's own tasks are
note   excluded. Read between runs, never inside a timed interval.
note   X BLOCK CASE PH PID TID COMM CPU STATE   a task last on core N (any state), or runnable (R) or in
note                            uninterruptible sleep (D) on another CPU of the cluster; spaces in COMM
note                            become _
note   Y BLOCK CASE PH tasks=N cluster=N xrows=N core_foreign_runnable=N errors=N   the counts of the
note                            scan: every task read, those last on the cluster, the X rows, the R tasks
note                            on core N, and the task stat files that could not be parsed
note   K BLOCK CASE start=N end=N contaminated=0|1   core_foreign_runnable of the two scans; 1 when
note                            either is above 0
note   R REASON CASE ARM        refusals (also on stderr), REASON in kind label unlisted manifest
note                            missing nowant status output changed
note   E LOADAVG                after the last block
note   S rows=N ok=N fail=N refused=N
note Exit: 0 when every row is ok and nothing was refused; 1 otherwise; 2 bad usage. Contamination does
note not change the exit status; it is classified from the K and X rows.
om2
text tbin "/bin/"
text trbin "bin/"
text tslash "/"
text twant "/want/"
text tdsha ".sha256"
text tin "/in/"
text trout "/run.out"
text trerr "/run.err"
text tman "/manifest.sha256"
text tnull "/dev/null"
text tload "/proc/loadavg"
text tstat "/proc/self/status"
text tcpus "Cpus_allowed_list:"
text tgcc "GCC: ("
text tdd "--"
text tsp " "
text tsp2 "  "
text tnl "\n"
text tH "H ngbench v2 blocks="
text twarm " warm="
text tcpu " cpus="
text tld " load="
text tA "A "
text tabs " absent"
text tI "I "
text tL "L "
text tT "T "
text tR "R "
text tE "E "
text tS "S rows="
text tok " ok="
text tfail " fail="
text tref " refused="
text tnrd "ngbench: cannot read "
text tusage "usage: ngbench sum FILE .. | ngbench run BLOCKS WARM DIR ARM .. -- CASE ..\n"
text trkind "kind"
text trlab "label"
text trunl "unlisted"
text trman "manifest"
text trmis "missing"
text trnow "nowant"
text trsta "status"
text trout2 "output"
text trchg "changed"
text tproc "/proc"
text ttask "/task"
text tstat2 "/stat"
text tsys1 "/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu"
text tsys2 "/topology/cluster_cpus_list"
text tcore " core="
text tunp "unpinned"
text tcm " clustermask="
text tX "X "
text tY "Y "
text tK "K "
text tphs "s"
text tphe "e"
text ttsk " tasks="
text tclu " cluster="
text txr " xrows="
text tcfr " core_foreign_runnable="
text terrs " errors="
text tkst " start="
text tken " end="
text tkc " contaminated="
note gpb: the path being built; gpk: the exec packet; glb: the output line; gfb: a whole file
note (binaries, manifest pieces, small text files); gmb: the manifest; gwx: want hex per case;
note ghx: hex of gdg, the last digest; gpr: present flags [case*16+arm]; gpl/gord: arm order
global gpb uchar 2048
global gpbn ulong 1
global gpk uchar 4096
global gpkn ulong 1
global gpkc ulong 1
global glb uchar 4096
global glbn ulong 1
global gfb uchar 16777216
global gmb uchar 1048576
global gmbn ulong 1
global gab uchar 256
global gdg uchar 32
global ghx uchar 64
global gwx uchar 4096
global gst uchar 4
global gstat ulong 1
global gpr ulong 1024
global gsz ulong 1024
global gpl ulong 16
global gord ulong 32
global gcfg ulong 16
global gcnt ulong 8
global gdn uchar 65536
global gdt uchar 65536
global gtb uchar 1024
global gsc ulong 16
note gsc: 0 timed core (99999 unpinned), 1 cluster mask, 2 own pid, 3 foreign R on the core, 4 tasks
note read, 5 tasks on the cluster, 6 X rows, 7 parse errors, 8 state byte, 9 cpu, 10/11 comm start/end
note gcfg: 0 blocks, 1 warm, 2 DIR arg index, 3 first arm arg, 4 arm count, 5 first case arg,
note 6 case count, 7 inproc line valid. gcnt: 0 rows, 1 ok, 2 fail, 3 refused.

note ---- path builder
fn pbclr to void
put gpbn 0 0
end
fn pbtext t view uchar * to void
n = get gpbn 0
if gt add n len t 2048
trap 9
end
for i ulong len t
put gpb add n i get t i
end
put gpbn 0 add n len t
end
fn pbarg idx ulong to void
n = get gpbn 0
r = argread idx gpb n sub 2048 n
if lt r 0
trap 9
end
put gpbn 0 add n ulong r
end
note DIR/T1 ARM T2 CASE T3, with any piece left out by passing index 0 / an empty text
fn pbdir to void
pbclr
pbarg get gcfg 2
end
fn pbbin ai ulong ci ulong to void
pbdir
pbtext tbin
pbarg ai
pbtext tslash
pbarg ci
end

note ---- exec packet: u16 count, then records (u16 length, bytes); pkpush adds gpb as one record
fn pkreset to void
put gpk 0 0
put gpk 1 0
put gpkn 0 2
put gpkc 0 0
end
fn pkpush to void
n = get gpkn 0
m = get gpbn 0
if gt add add n m 2 4096
trap 9
end
put gpk n uchar and m 255
put gpk add n 1 uchar shr m 8
for i ulong m
put gpk add add n 2 i get gpb i
end
put gpkn 0 add add n m 2
c = add get gpkc 0 1
put gpkc 0 c
put gpk 0 uchar and c 255
put gpk 1 uchar shr c 8
end

note ---- the output line
fn lbtext t view uchar * to void
n = get glbn 0
if gt add n len t 4096
trap 9
end
for i ulong len t
put glb add n i get t i
end
put glbn 0 add n len t
end
fn lbnum v ulong to void
d = new uchar 24 0
p = ulong 24
x = v
while gt x 9
p = sub p 1
put d p uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
end
p = sub p 1
put d p uchar add x 48
n = get glbn 0
for i ulong sub 24 p
put glb add n i get d add p i
end
put glbn 0 add n sub 24 p
end
fn lbarg idx ulong to void
n = get glbn 0
r = argread idx glb n sub 4096 n
if lt r 0
trap 9
end
put glbn 0 add n ulong r
end
fn lbhex to void
n = get glbn 0
if gt add n 64 4096
trap 9
end
for i ulong 64
put glb add n i get ghx i
end
put glbn 0 add n 64
end
note one line of gfb from st0, up to (not including) LF or the end n
fn lbfb st0 ulong n ulong to void
i = st0
going = true
while going
if ge i n
going = false
else
c = get gfb i
if eq c 10
going = false
else
m = get glbn 0
if lt m 4000
put glb m c
put glbn 0 add m 1
end
i = add i 1
end
end
end
end
fn lbsp to void
lbtext tsp
end
fn lbflush fd int to void
lbtext tnl
w = write fd glb 0 get glbn 0
put glbn 0 0
end

note ---- files: rdfb reads the file named by gpb into gfb; returns its size, 16777217 when it does not
note fit, 16777218 when it cannot be opened
fn rdfb to ulong
fd = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
ret 16777218
end
n = ulong 0
going = true
while going
r = read int fd gfb n sub 16777216 n
if le r 0
going = false
else
n = add n ulong r
if eq n 16777216
going = false
end
end
end
c = fclose int fd
if eq n 16777216
ret 16777217
end
ret n
end
note hashpb: SHA-256 of the file named by gpb into gdg and ghx; returns its size, or 2^63 when it
note cannot be opened or read
fn hashpb to ulong
b = new uchar 65536 0
c = new ulong 40 0
o = new uchar 32 0
fd = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
ret 9223372036854775808
end
sha256_init c
n = ulong 0
bad = false
going = true
while going bound 999999999
r = read int fd b 0 65536
if lt r 0
bad = true
going = false
else
if eq r 0
going = false
else
sha256_update c part b 0 ulong r
n = add n ulong r
end
end
end
x = fclose int fd
sha256_final c o
for i ulong 32
put gdg i get o i
end
tohex
if bad
ret 9223372036854775808
end
ret n
end
fn hexd v ulong to uchar
if lt v 10
ret uchar add v 48
end
ret uchar add v 87
end
fn tohex to void
for i ulong 32
v = ulong get gdg i
put ghx shl i 1 hexd shr v 4
put ghx add shl i 1 1 hexd and v 15
end
end

note ---- refusals and counts
fn refuse why view uchar * ci ulong ai ulong to void
lbtext tR
lbtext why
lbsp
lbarg ci
lbsp
if gt ai 0
lbarg ai
end
lbtext tnl
n = get glbn 0
w = write 2 glb 0 n
w = write 1 glb 0 n
put glbn 0 0
put gcnt 3 add get gcnt 3 1
end

note ---- arm kind from its name: 1 omc, 2 gcc, 3 ng, 0 unknown
fn armkind ai ulong to ulong
r = argread ai gab 0 len gab
if lt r 2
ret 0
end
a0 = get gab 0
a1 = get gab 1
if and eq a0 110 eq a1 103
ret 3
end
if lt r 3
ret 0
end
a2 = get gab 2
if and and eq a0 111 eq a1 109 eq a2 99
ret 1
end
if and and eq a0 103 eq a1 99 eq a2 99
ret 2
end
ret 0
end
note gfb[0..n) holds "GCC: (" somewhere: 1, else 0
fn hasgcc n ulong to ulong
if lt n 6
ret 0
end
for i ulong sub n 5 bound 16777216
if eq get gfb i 71
if fbmat i tgcc
ret 1
end
end
end
ret 0
end
fn u16at o ulong to ulong
ret or ulong get gfb o shl ulong get gfb add o 1 8
end
note the binary in gfb[0..n) matches kind: 1 yes, 0 no
fn kindok kind ulong n ulong to ulong
if lt n 64
ret 0
end
if ne get gfb 0 127
ret 0
end
if ne get gfb 1 69
ret 0
end
if ne get gfb 2 76
ret 0
end
if ne get gfb 3 70
ret 0
end
if ne u16at 18 183
ret 0
end
g = hasgcc n
if eq kind 2
ret g
end
if eq g 1
ret 0
end
if eq kind 3
ret 1
end
note omc: entry 0x4000b0 (bytes 24..31) and no section table (e_shoff, bytes 40..47, zero)
if ne u16at 24 176
ret 0
end
if ne u16at 26 64
ret 0
end
for i ulong 2
if ne u16at add 28 shl i 1 0
ret 0
end
end
for i ulong 8
if ne get gfb add 40 i 0
ret 0
end
end
ret 1
end

note ---- manifest: gmb holds DIR/manifest.sha256. mfind looks for the line whose path is
note bin/ARM/CASE: 0 not listed, 1 listed with hash ghx, 2 listed with another hash
fn mfind ai ulong ci ulong to ulong
p = new uchar 1024 0
put gpbn 0 0
pbtext trbin
pbarg ai
pbtext tslash
pbarg ci
m = get gpbn 0
for i ulong m
put p i get gpb i
end
n = get gmbn 0
s = ulong 0
while lt s n bound 999999999
e = s
while and lt e n ne get gmb e 10 bound 999999999
e = add e 1
end
if eq sub e s add 66 m
if msame s m p
ret mhash s
end
end
s = add e 1
end
ret 0
end
fn msame s ulong m ulong p view uchar 1024 to bool
for i ulong m
if ne get gmb add add s 66 i get p i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn mhash s ulong to ulong
for i ulong 64
if ne get gmb add s i get ghx i
ret 2
end
end
ret 1
end
fn mload to ulong
pbdir
pbtext tman
n = rdfb
if ge n 1048576
ret 0
end
for i ulong n bound 1048576
put gmb i get gfb i
end
put gmbn 0 n
ret 1
end

note ---- identity of every (case, arm); pass 0 before timing, 1 after (hashes must be unchanged)
fn ident pass ulong to void
na = get gcfg 4
for c ulong get gcfg 6
ci = add get gcfg 5 c
for a ulong na
ai = add get gcfg 3 a
slot = add shl c 4 a
if eq pass 0
identone ci ai slot
else
if eq get gpr slot 1
recheck ci ai slot
end
end
end
end
end
fn recheck ci ulong ai ulong slot ulong to void
pbbin ai ci
n = hashpb
k = mfind ai ci
if or ne n get gsz slot ne k 1
refuse trchg ci ai
put gpr slot 0
end
end
fn identone ci ulong ai ulong slot ulong to void
put gpr slot 0
pbbin ai ci
n = hashpb
if ge n 9223372036854775808
if ne mfind ai ci 0
refuse trmis ci ai
end
rowcase tA ci ai
lbtext tabs
lbflush 1
ret
end
k = mfind ai ci
if eq k 0
refuse trunl ci ai
ret
end
if eq k 2
refuse trman ci ai
ret
end
pbbin ai ci
nf = rdfb
if gt nf 16777216
refuse trlab ci ai
ret
end
if ne kindok armkind ai nf 1
refuse trlab ci ai
ret
end
put gsz slot n
put gpr slot 1
rowcase tA ci ai
lbsp
lbhex
lbsp
lbnum n
lbflush 1
end
fn rowcase t view uchar * ci ulong ai ulong to void
lbtext t
lbarg ci
lbsp
lbarg ai
end
note want hex and optional stdin of every case
fn wants to void
for c ulong get gcfg 6
ci = add get gcfg 5 c
pbdir
pbtext twant
pbarg ci
pbtext tdsha
n = rdfb
bad = or lt n 64 gt n 16777216
if not bad
for i ulong 64
v = get gfb i
isd = and ge v 48 le v 57
isl = and ge v 97 le v 102
if not or isd isl
bad = true
end
put gwx add shl c 6 i v
end
end
if bad
refuse trnow ci 0
end
pbdir
pbtext tin
pbarg ci
n2 = hashpb
if lt n2 9223372036854775808
lbtext tI
lbarg ci
lbsp
lbhex
lbsp
lbnum n2
lbflush 1
end
end
end

note ---- one child: stdin DIR/in/CASE or /dev/null, stdout DIR/run.out, stderr DIR/run.err, exec gpk
fn child ci ulong to void
pbdir
pbtext tin
pbarg ci
fi = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 0 0
if lt fi 0
fi = fopen tnull 0 len tnull 0 0
end
if lt fi 0
exit 122
end
r = dupfd int fi 0 0
if ne r 0
exit 123
end
pbdir
pbtext trout
fo = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 577 420
if lt fo 0
exit 120
end
r = dupfd int fo 1 0
if ne r 1
exit 121
end
pbdir
pbtext trerr
fe = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 577 420
if lt fe 0
exit 126
end
r = dupfd int fe 2 0
if ne r 2
exit 127
end
r = execprog gpk 0 get gpkn 0
exit 124
end
fn runone ci ulong to ulong
t0 = monons
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
trap 9
end
if eq pid 0
child ci
exit 125
end
r = waitpid int pid gst 0 4 0
t1 = monons
if ne r pid
trap 9
end
s0 = ulong get gst 0
if ne and s0 127 0
put gstat 0 add 1000 and s0 127
else
put gstat 0 ulong get gst 1
end
ret ulong sub t1 t0
end
note the n bytes of gfb must be 1 .. 19 digits and one LF; gcfg 7 is 1 when they are
fn rtparse n ulong to ulong
put gcfg 7 0
if or lt n 2 gt n 20
ret 0
end
if ne get gfb sub n 1 10
ret 0
end
v = ulong 0
for i ulong sub n 1
c = get gfb i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 0
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
end
put gcfg 7 1
ret v
end
note gcfg 8 wall ns, 9 status, 10 output ok, 11 in-process ns of the last run
fn dotime b ulong c ulong ai ulong pos ulong to void
ci = add get gcfg 5 c
pkreset
pbbin ai ci
pkpush
wall = runone ci
put gcfg 8 wall
put gcfg 9 get gstat 0
ok = outok c
put gcfg 10 ok
pbdir
pbtext trerr
ne2 = rdfb
rt = rtparse ne2
put gcfg 11 rt
trow b ci ai pos
tcount ci ai
end
fn outok c ulong to ulong
pbdir
pbtext trout
n = hashpb
if ge n 9223372036854775808
ret 0
end
for i ulong 64
if ne get ghx i get gwx add shl c 6 i
ret 0
end
end
ret 1
end
fn trow b ulong ci ulong ai ulong pos ulong to void
lbtext tT
lbnum b
lbsp
if lt b get gcfg 1
lbnum 1
else
lbnum 0
end
lbsp
lbarg ci
lbsp
lbarg ai
lbsp
lbnum pos
lbsp
lbnum get gcfg 8
lbsp
lbnum get gcfg 9
lbsp
if ne get gcfg 9 0
lbnum 0
else
lbnum get gcfg 10
end
lbsp
lbnum get gcfg 11
lbflush 1
end
fn tcount ci ulong ai ulong to void
put gcnt 0 add get gcnt 0 1
if ne get gcfg 9 0
refuse trsta ci ai
put gcnt 2 add get gcnt 2 1
ret
end
if eq get gcfg 10 0
refuse trout2 ci ai
put gcnt 2 add get gcnt 2 1
ret
end
put gcnt 1 add get gcnt 1 1
end
fn block b ulong to void
lbtext tL
lbnum b
lbsp
lbload
lbflush 1
na = get gcfg 4
for c ulong get gcfg 6
np = ulong 0
for a ulong na
if eq get gpr add shl c 4 a 1
put gpl np add get gcfg 3 a
np = add np 1
end
end
if gt np 0
for i ulong np
put gord i get gpl rem add i b np
end
for i ulong np
put gord add np i get gord sub sub np 1 i
end
sa = scanph b c 0
for p ulong shl np 1
dotime b c get gord p p
end
se = scanph b c 1
krow b c sa se
end
end
end

note ---- v2 contamination scan (PREREG-contamination.md)
fn pbnum v ulong to void
d = new uchar 24 0
p = ulong 24
x = v
while gt x 9
p = sub p 1
put d p uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
end
p = sub p 1
put d p uchar add x 48
n = get gpbn 0
if gt add n sub 24 p 2048
trap 9
end
for i ulong sub 24 p
put gpb add n i get d add p i
end
put gpbn 0 add n sub 24 p
end
note the timed core from Cpus_allowed_list (one number, else unpinned) and its cluster mask
fn coreset to void
put gsc 0 99999
put gsc 1 0
put gsc 2 ulong getpid
pbclr
pbtext tstat
n = rdfb
if gt n 16777216
ret
end
m = len tcpus
if lt n m
ret
end
for i ulong sub n m bound 16777216
if fbmat i tcpus
v = cpuone fbskip add i m n n
if lt v 64
put gsc 0 v
clusset v
end
ret
end
end
end
note the decimal at gfb[j ..] ended by LF; 99999 when anything else is there
fn cpuone j0 ulong n ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
j = j0
while lt j n bound 64
c = get gfb j
if eq c 10
if eq k 0
ret 99999
end
ret v
end
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 99999
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
k = add k 1
j = add j 1
end
ret 99999
end
fn clusset v ulong to void
pbclr
pbtext tsys1
pbnum v
pbtext tsys2
n = rdfb
if gt n 4096
put gsc 1 shl ulong 1 v
ret
end
put gsc 1 cpumask n
end
note a Linux cpu list (a-b,c,..) in gfb[0 .. n) as a mask of CPUs below 64
fn cpumask n ulong to ulong
m = ulong 0
a = ulong 0
lo = ulong 99999
have = false
for i ulong n
c = get gfb i
if and ge c 48 le c 57
a = add mul a 10 ulong sub c 48
have = true
else
if eq c 45
lo = a
a = 0
else
if have
m = or m rng lo a
end
lo = 99999
a = 0
have = false
end
end
end
if have
m = or m rng lo a
end
ret m
end
fn rng lo0 ulong hi ulong to ulong
lo = lo0
if eq lo 99999
lo = hi
end
m = ulong 0
k = lo
while and le k hi lt k 64 bound 64
m = or m shl ulong 1 k
k = add k 1
end
ret m
end
note one scan; returns the foreign runnable tasks on the timed core (0 when unpinned: no rows)
fn scanph b ulong c ulong ph ulong to ulong
if eq get gsc 0 99999
ret 0
end
put gsc 12 b
put gsc 13 c
put gsc 14 ph
put gsc 3 0
put gsc 4 0
put gsc 5 0
put gsc 6 0
put gsc 7 0
fd = fopen tproc 0 len tproc 0 0
if lt fd 0
put gsc 7 1
yrow
ret 0
end
going = true
while going bound 1000000
n = getdnts int fd gdn 0 65536
if le n 0
going = false
else
dnwalk ulong n
end
end
r = fclose int fd
yrow
ret get gsc 3
end
note the getdents64 records of gdn[0 .. n): d_reclen at 16 (u16), d_name at 19, zero-terminated
fn dnwalk n ulong to void
o = ulong 0
while lt o n bound 1000000
rl = or ulong get gdn add o 16 shl ulong get gdn add o 17 8
pid = dnum o
if ne pid 18446744073709551615
taskdir pid
end
if eq rl 0
o = n
else
o = add o rl
end
end
end
fn dnum o ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
i = add o 19
while and lt i 65536 ne get gdn i 0 bound 300
c = get gdn i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 18446744073709551615
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
i = add i 1
k = add k 1
end
if eq k 0
ret 18446744073709551615
end
ret v
end
fn tnum o ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
i = add o 19
while and lt i 65536 ne get gdt i 0 bound 300
c = get gdt i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 18446744073709551615
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
i = add i 1
k = add k 1
end
if eq k 0
ret 18446744073709551615
end
ret v
end
note /proc/PID/task: a process that exited since the /proc listing is skipped (a normal race)
fn taskdir pid ulong to void
pbclr
pbtext tproc
pbtext tslash
pbnum pid
pbtext ttask
fd = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
going = true
while going bound 1000000
n = getdnts int fd gdt 0 65536
if le n 0
going = false
else
tdwalk ulong n pid
end
end
r = fclose int fd
end
fn tdwalk n ulong pid ulong to void
o = ulong 0
while lt o n bound 1000000
rl = or ulong get gdt add o 16 shl ulong get gdt add o 17 8
tid = tnum o
if ne tid 18446744073709551615
taskone pid tid
end
if eq rl 0
o = n
else
o = add o rl
end
end
end
fn taskone pid ulong tid ulong to void
pbclr
pbtext tproc
pbtext tslash
pbnum pid
pbtext ttask
pbtext tslash
pbnum tid
pbtext tstat2
fd = fopen gpb 0 get gpbn 0 0 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
n = read int fd gtb 0 1024
r = fclose int fd
if le n 0
ret
end
put gsc 4 add get gsc 4 1
if not tparse ulong n
put gsc 7 add get gsc 7 1
ret
end
taskdec pid tid
end
fn taskdec pid ulong tid ulong to void
cpu = get gsc 9
incl = false
if lt cpu 64
incl = eq and shr get gsc 1 cpu 1 1
end
if incl
put gsc 5 add get gsc 5 1
end
if eq pid get gsc 2
ret
end
st = get gsc 8
if eq cpu get gsc 0
if eq st 82
put gsc 3 add get gsc 3 1
end
xrow pid tid
ret
end
if and incl or eq st 82 eq st 68
xrow pid tid
end
end
note gtb[0 .. n): PID (COMM) STATE ... ; COMM is up to the last ')'; field 39 (processor) is the 37th
note space-separated field from STATE
fn tparse n ulong to bool
p1 = n
p2 = n
for i ulong n
c = get gtb i
if and eq c 40 eq p1 n
p1 = i
end
if eq c 41
p2 = i
end
end
if or ge p1 n ge add p2 3 n
ret false
end
put gsc 10 add p1 1
put gsc 11 p2
put gsc 8 ulong get gtb add p2 2
ret tcpufld add p2 2 n
end
fn tcpufld j0 ulong n ulong to bool
j = j0
k = ulong 1
while and lt j n lt k 37 bound 2048
if eq get gtb j 32
k = add k 1
end
j = add j 1
end
if lt k 37
ret false
end
v = ulong 0
d = ulong 0
going = true
while and going lt j n bound 32
c = get gtb j
if and ge c 48 le c 57
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
d = add d 1
j = add j 1
else
going = false
end
end
if eq d 0
ret false
end
put gsc 9 v
ret true
end
note BLOCK CASE PH of the current scan (gsc 12, 13, 14)
fn lbbcp to void
lbnum get gsc 12
lbsp
lbarg add get gcfg 5 get gsc 13
lbsp
if eq get gsc 14 0
lbtext tphs
else
lbtext tphe
end
end
fn xrow pid ulong tid ulong to void
lbtext tX
lbbcp
lbsp
lbnum pid
lbsp
lbnum tid
lbsp
lbcomm
lbsp
lbnum get gsc 9
lbsp
m = get glbn 0
put glb m uchar get gsc 8
put glbn 0 add m 1
lbflush 1
put gsc 6 add get gsc 6 1
end
fn lbcomm to void
s = get gsc 10
e = get gsc 11
for i ulong sub e s
c = get gtb add s i
if or le c 32 ge c 127
c = 95
end
m = get glbn 0
if lt m 4000
put glb m c
put glbn 0 add m 1
end
end
end
fn yrow to void
lbtext tY
lbbcp
lbtext ttsk
lbnum get gsc 4
lbtext tclu
lbnum get gsc 5
lbtext txr
lbnum get gsc 6
lbtext tcfr
lbnum get gsc 3
lbtext terrs
lbnum get gsc 7
lbflush 1
end
fn krow b ulong c ulong sa ulong se ulong to void
if eq get gsc 0 99999
ret
end
lbtext tK
lbnum b
lbsp
lbarg add get gcfg 5 c
lbtext tkst
lbnum sa
lbtext tken
lbnum se
lbtext tkc
if or gt sa 0 gt se 0
lbnum 1
else
lbnum 0
end
lbflush 1
end

note ---- /proc readers
fn lbload to void
pbclr
pbtext tload
n = rdfb
if gt n 16777216
ret
end
lbfb 0 n
end
fn lbcpus to void
pbclr
pbtext tstat
n = rdfb
if gt n 16777216
ret
end
m = len tcpus
if lt n m
ret
end
for i ulong sub n m bound 16777216
if fbmat i tcpus
j = fbskip add i m n
lbfb j n
ret
end
end
end
note gfb[i ..] starts with t (the caller keeps i + len t inside the buffer)
fn fbmat i ulong t view uchar * to bool
for k ulong len t
if ne get gfb add i k get t k
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn fbskip j0 ulong n ulong to ulong
j = j0
while lt j n
c = get gfb j
if and ne c 9 ne c 32
ret j
end
j = add j 1
end
ret j
end

note ---- arguments
fn argnum idx ulong to ulong
r = argread idx gab 0 len gab
if or le r 0 gt r 18
exit 2
end
v = ulong 0
for i ulong ulong r
c = get gab i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
exit 2
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
end
ret v
end
fn usage to void
w = write 2 tusage 0 len tusage
exit 2
end
fn isdd idx ulong to bool
r = argread idx gab 0 len gab
if ne r 2
ret false
end
ret and eq get gab 0 45 eq get gab 1 45
end
fn setup to void
ac = ulong argcnt
if lt ac 8
usage
end
put gcfg 0 argnum 2
put gcfg 1 argnum 3
if eq get gcfg 0 0
usage
end
if gt add get gcfg 0 get gcfg 1 100000
usage
end
put gcfg 2 4
put gcfg 3 5
k = ulong 5
fd = false
while and lt k ac not fd
if isdd k
fd = true
else
k = add k 1
end
end
if not fd
usage
end
na = sub k 5
if or eq na 0 gt na 16
usage
end
nc = sub ac add k 1
if or eq nc 0 gt nc 64
usage
end
put gcfg 4 na
put gcfg 5 add k 1
put gcfg 6 nc
for a ulong na
if eq armkind add 5 a 0
usage
end
end
end
fn summary to int
lbtext tE
lbload
lbflush 1
lbtext tS
lbnum get gcnt 0
lbtext tok
lbnum get gcnt 1
lbtext tfail
lbnum get gcnt 2
lbtext tref
lbnum get gcnt 3
lbflush 1
if or ne get gcnt 2 0 ne get gcnt 3 0
ret 1
end
if eq get gcnt 1 0
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
fn dosum to int
bad = int 0
for i ulong sub ulong argcnt 2
ai = add i 2
pbclr
pbarg ai
n = hashpb
if ge n 9223372036854775808
lbtext tnrd
lbarg ai
lbtext tnl
w = write 2 glb 0 get glbn 0
put glbn 0 0
bad = 1
else
lbhex
lbtext tsp2
lbarg ai
lbflush 1
end
end
ret bad
end
fn dorun to int
setup
lbtext tH
lbnum get gcfg 0
lbtext twarm
lbnum get gcfg 1
lbtext tcpu
lbcpus
coreset
lbtext tcore
if eq get gsc 0 99999
lbtext tunp
else
lbnum get gsc 0
end
lbtext tcm
lbnum get gsc 1
lbtext tld
lbload
lbflush 1
if eq mload 0
refuse trman get gcfg 2 0
ret summary
end
wants
ident 0
if ne get gcnt 3 0
ret summary
end
for b ulong add get gcfg 0 get gcfg 1
block b
end
ident 1
ret summary
end
fn main to int
if lt argcnt 3
usage
end
r = argread 1 gab 0 len gab
if eq r 3
if and and eq get gab 0 115 eq get gab 1 117 eq get gab 2 109
ret dosum
end
if and and eq get gab 0 114 eq get gab 1 117 eq get gab 2 110
ret dorun
end
end
usage
ret 2
end

note ---- SHA-256: omega-mv 943d9555 om/tls/sha2.om (sha256 5cf0f981...6fdb33), verbatim below.
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note om/tls/sha2.om: SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512 (FIPS 180-4) streaming, as an OM-2 library unit
note (no om2 line, no main, no globals). Module code SH; functions sha2_*, sha256_*, sha384_*, sha512_*.
note
note API
note   sha256_init c edit ulong *            c: 40 ulong cells (caller owns all state)
note   sha256_update c edit ulong * m view uchar *   any length, any chunking
note   sha256_final c edit ulong * o edit uchar *    writes 32 bytes (o shorter traps 3)
note   sha384_* / sha512_* the same; final writes 48 / 64 bytes
note   sha2_copy d edit ulong * s view ulong *       copies len s cells (a context snapshot)
note   sha2_digest alg ulong m view uchar * o edit uchar * to ulong
note     alg 256|384|512: one-shot digest into o, returns 32|48|64; any other alg returns 0, writes nothing
note After final the context is spent (its state cells hold the last chaining value); init it again.
note A context initialised for one algorithm must be used with that algorithm's update/final; the
note common code reads the algorithm from cell 9, so sha256_update on a sha512 context hashes SHA-512.
note
note Context cells: 0..7 chaining value H (32-bit words zero-extended for SHA-256), 8 = bytes absorbed
note mod 2^64, 9 = algorithm (256, 384, 512), 16..31 = pending block bytes packed big-endian (byte i
note in cell 16 + i/8, bits 56 - 8*(i mod 8)), 10..15 and 32..39 = 0.
note Constant time: every branch, loop count and index depends only on lengths and the algorithm,
note never on message or state bytes. Local schedule/state/padding arrays are zeroed before return
note (HMAC keys pass through them). omc emits plain AArch64; MUL/ADD/EOR/ROR/shift data-independent.
note Message length: any length below 2^64 bytes; update cuts its input into runs of 2^25 bytes so no
note loop passes 2^20 times (a rolled for traps 4 after 10^6 passes; the while bound 999999 of runs
note allows inputs up to 999999 * 32 MiB per update call).

note K{256}[0..64): first 32 bits of the fractional parts of the cube roots of the first 64 primes
note (FIPS 180-4 4.2.2). Same values as om/sha256/sha256-om2.om; recomputed with Wolfram:
note IntegerString[Floor[FractionalPart[N[CubeRoot[Prime[i]],60]]*2^32],16,8] for i = 1..64.
